messages:
jonathan: quick question — i'm touching the payments helm chart and seeing an annoying helm templating issue. our infra pipeline creates an ExternalSecret and writes the secret name into values (values.secrets.payments). if that value is missing helm still emits an envFrom with name "" and the pod crashes. any neat guard patterns for nested map overrides so we don't produce an empty secretRef?

jonathan: simplified current template:
```
envFrom:
  - secretRef:
      name: {{ .Values.secrets.payments }}
```

jonathan: when values.secrets.payments is null/not set we end up with `name: ```. i want to avoid wrapping the whole env block in an if because we have multiple optional entries.

sam: TL;DR: guard the individual entries or build the list in a helper. e.g. simplest is per-entry if:
```
envFrom:|
{{- if .Values.secrets.payments }}
  - secretRef:
      name: {{ .Values.secrets.payments }}
{{- end }}
{{- if .Values.secrets.legacy }}
  - secretRef:
      name: {{ .Values.secrets.legacy }}
{{- end }}
```
sam: that prevents emitting an empty name. alternatively you can have a helper that returns the list and `toYaml` it.

maya: fwiw i usually build the slice in a tpl helper so templates don't get cluttered when there are many optional secrets:
```
{{- define "payments.secretRefs" -}}
{{- $refs := list -}}
{{- if .Values.secrets.payments }}
{{- $refs = append $refs (dict "name" .Values.secrets.payments) }}
{{- end }}
{{- if .Values.secrets.legacy }}
{{- $refs = append $refs (dict "name" .Values.secrets.legacy) }}
{{- end }}
{{- toYaml $refs | nindent 2 }}
{{- end }}

# usage:
envFrom:
{{ include "payments.secretRefs" . | indent 2 }}
```

maya: this keeps logic in one place and avoids missing-key issues.

jonathan: nice, i'll wire that in. secondary concern — terraform runs separately and might create the ExternalSecret after helm deploy. any ideas to avoid the race where helm renders nothing because tf hasn't set values yet?

sam: two approaches we've used:
- chart flag: add `externalSecret.enabled` and have the infra pipeline flip that once TF apply is done. infra applies ES, then the apps pipeline sets the flag and runs helm upgrade. deterministic.
- placeholder: render a placeholder secret name and rely on the ExternalSecret controller to reconcile — but placeholders must be valid names and are fragile.

maya: my vote is the flag + a small `kubectl wait` in infra to ensure the ExternalSecret CR exists before flipping. avoid using `lookup` in templates — it couples chart to cluster state and breaks `helm template`/dry-run.

sam: agreed — prefer not to use `lookup` unless you understand the implications for local templating.

deploy-bot: deploy-bot: proposal: infra pipeline creates ExternalSecret first, then writes a small marker file in S3 that the apps pipeline reads to set `externalSecret.enabled=true` for the next helm upgrade. worked for us before.

jonathan: i'll implement the helper and add `externalSecret.enabled=false` default, plus docs on infra ordering. will open a PR.

maya: add a CHANGES note re ordering so oncall doesn't get surprised.

jonathan: created PR #432: https://git.internal/repo/pulls/432 — includes helper, a unit test for templates, and docs on infra ordering.

sam: LGTM, left two tiny nits. infra-bot: tagging infra team to coordinate the TF apply.

infra-bot: infra-team: FYI — please run TF apply and set `apps/deploy/flags/external-secrets/payments` before promoting helm to prod.

jonathan: thanks all :thumbsup:
